    {
      "text": "Esau ran to meet him … and they wept, Gen. 33:4. Joseph … entered into his chamber, and wept, Gen. 43:30. he wept aloud: and the Egyptians … heard, Gen. 45:2. Joseph … went up to meet Israel … and wept, Gen. 46:29. she saw the child: and, behold, the babe wept, Ex. 2:6. Hannah, why weepest thou, 1 Sam. 1:8. Saul said, What aileth the people that they weep, 1 Sam. 11:5. David and the people … wept, until they had no more power to weep, 1 Sam. 30:4. David went up … mount Olivet, and wept, 2 Sam. 15:30. ashamed: and the man of God wept, 2 Kgs. 8:11. Hezekiah wept sore, 2 Kgs. 20:3 (Isa. 38:3). time to weep, and a time to laugh, Eccl. 3:4. I will weep bitterly, Isa. 22:4. ambassadors of peace shall weep, Isa. 33:7. that I might weep day and night for the slain, Jer. 9:1. Rahel weeping for her children refused to be comforted, Jer. 31:15 (Matt. 2:18). Let the priests … weep, Joel 2:17.",
