      "text": "Peter … wept bitterly, Matt. 26:75 (Mark 14:72; Luke 22:62). Why … weep? the damsel is not dead, Mark 5:39 (Luke 8:52). Blessed are ye that weep, Luke 6:21. he beheld the city, and wept, Luke 19:41. weep not for me, but weep for yourselves, Luke 23:28. She goeth unto the grave to weep, John 11:31. Jesus wept, John 11:35. ye shall weep and lament, John 16:20. Mary stood without at the sepulchre weeping, John 20:11. What mean ye to weep and to break mine heart, Acts 21:13. weep with them that weep, Rom. 12:15. they that weep, as though they wept not, 1 Cor. 7:30. Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep, James 4:9. rich men, weep and howl for your miseries, James 5:1. I wept much, because no man was found worthy, Rev. 5:4.",
